ettings.","small_element_aria_label":"More info","tiny_element_one_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","tiny_element_two_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","tiny_element_aria_label":"Unblock <%=componentname%>","analytics":"analytics","functional":"functional","essential":"essential","advertising":"marketing"}},"comp-jw9fjw0w":{"html":"<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:20px;\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Method</span></span></span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-jw9fjw20":{"html":"<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Start by adding all of the marinade ingredients to a shallow saucepan and bring to a high bubbling simmer to reduce it by half and thicken the sauce.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">If using bamboo or other wooden skewers, soak them in water for 30 minutes before&nbsp;threading the chicken and onions onto them.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">While the sauce reduces, cut the chicken into approximately 1 by 2 inch pieces that are 1/4 to 1/2 inch thick. Skewer the chicken alternating with 1 inch pieces of green onion. Start with a piece of chicken. Fold it in half so you have a roughly 1 inch cube. Continue until you have around four pieces of chicken and three pieces of green onion per skewer if you use the short ones as I did.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">When the skewers are assembled, transfer the reduced sauce to a basting dish and get your grill heated&nbsp;to around 375 degrees.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Place the skewers on the grill and start basting.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Turn the skewers in quarter turns and baste again every 60 seconds or so.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">This keeps the chicken cooking evenly.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Keep basting until the chicken is firm and cooked through. (8-10 minutes)</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">We started ours on a pellet grill for additional smoky taste, then moved them to our little gas searing grill for just a few minutes to get a better caramelized exterior.&nbsp;Any grill you like to use will work for this recipe just turn up the temperature at the end if you like your yakitori with more caramelization.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-jw9fjw36":{"id":"comp-jw9fjw36","appDefinitionId":"13016589-a9eb-424a-8a69-46cb05ce0b2c","widgetId":"130165ba-4eeb-4a87-3121-a3cf2a86d2ca","isAppInClientSpecMap":true,"isViewerMode":true,"isResponsive":false,"translations":{"preloaderOverlay":{"loading":"Loading"},"errorMessageOverlay":{"reloadText":"Refresh this page","oopsText":"App Didn't Load","installErrorText":"We Were Unable to Install This App","generalErrorPrefix":"Try again later, disable any ad blockers, or reload the page. Contact the author of","generalErrorSuffix":"for help.","uninstalledErrorText":"We Were Unable to Install This App"},"unavailableMessageOverlay":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us.","relo